{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/placement"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/placement"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV9placementAA13MXLAboveBelowOSgvp","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAboveBelow","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"placement"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","text":"MXLAboveBelow","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"placement"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"title":"MXLArpeggiate","abstract":[{"text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLAboveBelow","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/placement":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/placement","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/placement","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAboveBelow","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAboveBelowO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"placement","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notation."}],"type":"topic"}}}